{% comment %}
  Circular Fash product card (Fashionphile-style) — replaces the Refresh
  card while keeping the same render interface, so featured-collection,
  main-collection-product-grid, search and related-products all pick it up.

  The previous customized card is preserved at
  snippets/WISHLIST_HERO_BKP_card-product-pre-cf.liquid.

  The condition line and the "Est. retail / % below retail" line were removed
  2026-08-08 at the client's request and restored 2026-08-25 at the client's
  request. The retail figure comes from the custom.retail_price metafield, not
  compare_at_price — see the comment beside it for why that distinction matters.
{% endcomment %}

{%- if card_product and card_product != empty -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign current_variant = card_product.selected_or_first_available_variant
    assign price = current_variant.price

    assign brand = ''
    if card_product.vendor != blank and card_product.vendor != shop.name
      assign brand = card_product.vendor
    endif

    assign display_title = card_product.title
    if brand != ''
      assign display_title = card_product.title | remove_first: brand | strip
      if display_title == ''
        assign display_title = card_product.title
      endif
    endif

    comment
      Sizes on the card, so a shopper never has to open a product to find out
      it isn't their size. The catalogue names this option inconsistently
      (Size / Taille / Storlek), and sizes are read off the variants rather
      than option.values so sold-out sizes of a part-sold product stay hidden.
    endcomment
    assign size_index = 0
    for option in card_product.options_with_values
      assign option_name = option.name | downcase
      if option_name contains 'size' or option_name contains 'taille' or option_name contains 'storlek'
        assign size_index = forloop.index
      endif
    endfor

    assign size_list = ''
    if size_index > 0
      for variant in card_product.variants
        if variant.available
          assign size_value = ''
          case size_index
            when 1
              assign size_value = variant.option1
            when 2
              assign size_value = variant.option2
            when 3
              assign size_value = variant.option3
          endcase
          comment
            "One size" / "one-size" (140 variants) carries no information on a
            bag or wallet, so it is dropped and the row falls back to the
            spacer. Real sizes are kept exactly as the catalogue spells them.
          endcomment
          assign size_check = size_value | downcase | replace: '-', ' ' | replace: '_', ' ' | strip
          if size_value != blank and size_value != 'Default Title' and size_check != 'one size' and size_check != 'onesize' and size_check != 'os'
            assign size_list = size_list | append: size_value | append: '~'
          endif
        endif
      endfor
    endif
    assign sizes = size_list | split: '~' | uniq
  -%}
  <div class="cf">{% render 'wishlisthero-collection-product' with product: card_product %}
    <a class="card" href="{{ card_product.url }}">
      {%- if card_product.available == false -%}
        <span class="seen">Sold</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      <div class="frame cf-slides" data-label="{{ card_product.title | escape }}">
        {%- if card_product.featured_media -%}
          <img
            class="main"
            srcset="{{ card_product.featured_media | image_url: width: 400 }} 400w, {{ card_product.featured_media | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w"
            src="{{ card_product.featured_media | image_url: width: 800 }}"
            sizes="(min-width: 990px) 320px, (min-width: 750px) 33vw, 50vw"
            alt="{{ card_product.featured_media.alt | escape }}"
            {% unless lazy_load == false %}loading="lazy"{% endunless %}
            width="{{ card_product.featured_media.width }}"
            height="{{ card_product.featured_media.height }}"
          >
          {%- if show_secondary_image -%}
            {%- for media in card_product.media offset: 1 limit: 3 -%}
              <img
                class="alt{% unless forloop.first %} extra{% endunless %}"
                src="{{ media | image_url: width: 800 }}"
                alt=""
                loading="lazy"
                width="{{ media.width }}"
                height="{{ media.height }}"
              >
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      <div class="card-info">
        {%- if brand != '' -%}
          <div class="brand">{{ brand }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
        <div class="pname">{{ display_title }}</div>
        {%- comment -%}
          Held open with a spacer when a piece has no size (bags, wallets) so
          prices stay on one line across the row.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          No placeholder when a piece has no size. Bags and wallets were
          holding open an invisible chip, a condition row and a retail row, so
          a card with none of the three carried three empty lines of nothing.
          The rows simply close up now.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if sizes.size > 0 -%}
          <div class="csize">{{ sizes | join: ' · ' }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Condition and "Est. retail / % below retail", restored. Both were on
          this card until 2026-08-08.

          The saving is measured against the retail metafield, NOT compare_at:
          they are different numbers and compare_at badly undersells. A Moncler
          Maya is 5 800 with compare_at 7 000, but retail is 18 000 — "17%
          off" against "68% below retail" for the same jacket.

          Empty rows are held open so prices stay on one line across a row,
          the same reason the size chip has a spacer.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign cond = card_product.metafields.custom.condition.value.name.value
          assign retail_raw = card_product.metafields.custom.retail_price.value
          assign price_kr = price | divided_by: 100
          assign show_retail = false
          if retail_raw != blank
            assign retail_num = retail_raw | plus: 0
            assign retail_round = retail_num | round
            if retail_round > 0 and price_kr < retail_round
              assign saved = retail_round | minus: price_kr
              assign pct = saved | times: 100 | divided_by: retail_round | round
              if pct > 0
                assign show_retail = true
              endif
            endif
          endif
        -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          No "Condition:" prefix on the card. At two columns on a phone the
          card is ~175px and "Condition: 10/10 - New with Tags" wraps to two
          lines, while a shorter grade stays on one, which staggers the prices
          across a row. The grade reads as a grade without being labelled, and
          the product page carries the labelled version. Fashionphile prints
          the bare grade on its cards for the same reason.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if cond != blank -%}
          <div class="cond">{{ cond }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="price">{{ price | money }}</div>

        {%- if show_retail -%}
          <div class="retail-line">
            Est. retail
            <span data-retail-sek="{{ retail_round }}">{{ retail_round }} SEK</span>
            · <b>{{ pct }}% below retail</b>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </a>
  </div>
{%- else -%}
  <div class="cf">
    <a class="card" href="#">
      <div class="frame" data-label="Product"></div>
      <div class="card-info">
        <div class="pname">Example product</div>
        <div class="price">{{ 1999 | money }}</div>
      </div>
    </a>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
